{"created": "2022-01-26T22:08:43.501070+00:00", "modified": "2022-06-05T06:46:49.996783+00:00", "id": 5904586, "conceptrecid": "5904585", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.5904586", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.5904585", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5904586", "metadata": {"title": "APL synapses distribution on PN and KC meshes, primary data, calcium imaging macros and python scripts from Prisco et al.", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.5904586", "publication_date": "2022-01-26", "description": "<p class=\"MsoBodyText\">To identify and memorize discrete but similar environmental inputs, the brain needs to distinguish between subtle differences of activity patterns in defined neuronal populations. The Kenyon cells of the <i>Drosophila </i>adult mushroom body (MB) respond sparsely to complex olfactory input, a property that is thought to support stimuli discrimination in the MB. To understand how this property emerges, we investigated the role of the inhibitory anterior paired lateral neuron (APL) in the input circuit of the MB, the calyx. Within the calyx, presynaptic boutons of projection neurons (PNs) form large synaptic microglomeruli (MGs) with dendrites of postsynaptic Kenyon cells (KCs). Combining EM data analysis and <i>in vivo</i> calcium imaging, we show that APL, via inhibitory and reciprocal synapses targeting both PN boutons and KC dendrites, normalizes odour-evoked representations in MGs of the calyx. APL response scales with the PN input strength and is regionalized around PN input distribution. Our data indicate that the formation of a sparse code by the Kenyon cells requires APL-driven normalization of their MG postsynaptic responses. This work provides experimental insights on how inhibition shapes sensory information representation in a higher brain centre, thereby supporting stimuli discrimination and allowing for efficient associative memory formation.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Tavosanis, Gaia", "affiliation": "University of Bonn", "orcid": "0000-0002-8679-5515"}, {"name": "Prisco, Luigi", "affiliation": "German Center for Neurodegenerative Diseases", "orcid": "0000-0002-5896-9346"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.7554/eLife.74172", "relation": "isCitedBy", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5061/dryad.bk3j9kdd1", "relation": "isSourceOf", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "communities": [{"id": "dryad"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "5904585"}}]}, "notes": "<p>This dataset contains all the source data contained in Prisco et al.,\u00a0sorted\u00a0by Figure.</p>"}, "title": "APL synapses distribution on PN and KC meshes, primary data, calcium imaging macros and python scripts from Prisco et al.", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5904586", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5904586", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5904586?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5904586", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5904586", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.5904586", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5904586/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5904585", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5904585", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5904585", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.5904585", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:5904586/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:5904586/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5904586/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5904586/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5904586/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5904586/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5904586/versions/latest", "lat